Clean-room format and documentation sources
===========================================

This package decodes EDF files written by a ResMed AirSense 11 to SD card. It
was implemented from the published European Data Format specification and from
project documentation, with no third-party runtime dependency:

* The EDF/EDF+ specification published at edfplus.info, which defines the
  256-byte header record, the ns x 256-byte signal header block, the ASCII
  field widths, and the little-endian 16-bit data records.
* docs/integration/hms-cpap-ezshare-integration.md
* docs/integration/resmed-air11-ble-stream.md, for the channel set and the
  canonical units already settled for the Bluetooth path.
* vitals/registry.toml, the single source of truth for every type, canonical
  unit and valid range.
* openspec/changes/cpap-ezshare-ingest/{proposal,design,tasks}.md

No OSCAR or hms-cpap implementation code was read or copied. OSCAR is
GPL-licensed and this project does not copy GPL implementation code; its
documentation of ResMed's *file formats* informed the channel label and
dimension spellings in channels.py, which the change proposal explicitly
permits as formats-only.

No third-party EDF library is used. pyedflib and cpap-py were both considered
and rejected: see the frozen decision recorded under T-CP2 in
openspec/changes/cpap-ezshare-ingest/tasks.md. The short form is that these
bytes arrive from an untrusted SD card over unauthenticated HTTP, and handing
them to a compiled C extension would reverse the memory-safety property the
mirror in batch/cpap_ezshare exists to establish.

Python standard-library modules are the only runtime dependencies: dataclasses,
hashlib, pathlib, re and tomllib.

ResMed, AirSense and ez Share names identify their respective products. No
affiliation or endorsement is implied.
